    title: "Leading Across Differences",
    duration: "15–20 min",
    hook: "The most innovative, highest-performing teams are consistently diverse — in background, perspective, and experience. But diverse teams are also frequently the hardest to lead. Cultural differences in communication style, authority relationships, time orientation, and conflict expression can produce misunderstanding, friction, and underperformance if not skillfully navigated. And the leader who can create cohesion across differences — building genuine inclusion rather than just tolerating diversity — is one of the most valuable people in any organization.",
