    title: "Courage in Leadership",
    duration: "15–20 min",
    hook: "Courage is not the absence of fear — it's acting rightly despite fear. Every leader who has done something genuinely important has done it while afraid. Afraid of failure, of judgment, of being wrong, of losing relationships or status. The difference between leaders who make a difference and those who don't is almost never capability or knowledge — it's the willingness to act courageously despite the risk. Understanding what leadership courage actually requires — and what blocks it — may be the most practically important thing you learn in this entire course.",
